            <ArticleTitle>Left internal mammary--left ventricular fistula after Vineberg operation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This communication presents an unusual complication in a patient who underwent the Vineberg procedure with the formation of an internal mammary to left-ventricular fistula, which caused a new apical diastolic murmur. This represents a previously unreported etiology for the appearance of an apical blowing diastolic murmur.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
